# Backend (route handlers & server libs)

## Existing surface (do not hallucinate more)

- **Route handlers** in this repo today live at:
  - `src/app/api/contact/route.ts` (message form)
  - `src/app/api/booking/route.ts` (availability and booking against Google Calendar)
- Do **not** add new `route.ts` files, path segments, or HTTP clients unless the user explicitly asks for a new endpoint or integration.

## Environment variables

- Only reference variables **already used** in code or named by the user. Examples that appear in the codebase include (non-exhaustive—**read the files**):
  - `RESEND_API_KEY`, `RESEND_NOREPLY_FROM`, `CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL` (contact email)
  - `CLOUDFLARE_SITE_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_SECRET_KEY` (Turnstile; optional locally, required in production)
  - `GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID`, `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL`, `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY` (booking; the route reports the calendar unavailable when unset)
- Never invent `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` secrets. Never add placeholder env names.

## Patterns to preserve

- There is no database in this repo. Email through `@/lib/resend-client` is the system of record for leads and Google Calendar (`@/lib/booking/google-calendar`) holds bookings; do not add a datastore without instruction.
- Keep **validation**, **payload size limits**, and **`NextResponse.json`** error shapes consistent with the existing `contact` and `booking` handlers.
- Preserve **HTML escaping** for email HTML in `contact` (or equivalent) when touching that path.

## Auth and “middleware”

- This marketing site does **not** ship a user session auth layer in code today. Do not add middleware-based auth enforcement or generic “JWT middleware” unless explicitly requested and designed.
- There is no auth in this repo. If it is introduced later, follow verified patterns documented in `.cursorrules`.

## Editing discipline

- Read both API files (and any shared `src/lib` helper you touch) before changing behavior.
- **Small edits**; no drive-by refactors across `src/lib`.
- **No unrelated deletions.**

## Deployment

- Assume **Vercel + Next** consistent with dependencies (`next`, `@vercel/analytics`). This repo has **no BigQuery**—do not add BigQuery or other backend services unless the task says so.
